Package: hourcalc
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: convert hours between h:mm and decimal hours, and calculate with hours
 HourCalc converts hours between hours and minutes (08:30) and decimal hours
 (8,50): type in either field and the other one follows at once. A second tab
 calculates with hours: it adds and subtracts durations and multiplies and
 divides them by a factor. The number of decimal places (2 to 6) and the
 theme (system, light or dark) are settings.
 .
 The program looks native on both major desktops. This package ships two front
 ends on one shared core: GTK 4 with libadwaita for GNOME and Qt 6 for KDE
 Plasma. The hourcalc command starts the one that fits the desktop; set
 HOURCALC_UI=gtk or HOURCALC_UI=qt to choose.
